# Ammonite-conch kraken body plan -- SHELL (K) casing SURROUNDS a MEAT (M)
# interior. Krakens carry no blubber; the game holds them aloft (a neutral-
# buoyancy exception), so there is no W and the float rule does not apply.
# Preview:  godot --headless --path . --script tools/ship_preview.gd -- ships/kraken_c.ship
#
# THE ANATOMY (owner, from the source, 2026-08-23): the shell is an OUTER
# CASING wrapping the beast; the MEAT is INSIDE; only a LITTLE meat is EXPOSED,
# as a deliberate GAMEPLAY WEAK SPOT. Shell is armored (hp 250, collision_resist
# 20), so shots barely dent it -- to hurt the kraken you must snipe the small
# exposed-meat tiles. This is the reworked C (owner: "C is closest in spirit,
# make it 'perfect'"): LONGER, a somewhat POINTY shell tip on the LEFT (the
# coiled ram tip), sweeping into a matched, similarly-sized MOUTH entrance on
# the RIGHT -- an aperture in the casing (no shell on the mouth side) that bares
# the throat. The only exterior meat is at that mouth (~3 tiles): the weak spot.
# Buried inside is a meat-walled LOOT CAVITY (like the whale stomach) -- mine
# through to reach it. One 4-connected body, no thin necks.
#
#   K shell (armour: hp 250, mass 2, collision_resist 20 -- light, very hard)
#   M meat  (dense flesh -- the interior body and the exposed mouth-throat)
#   . air / hollow (the open mouth aperture and the sealed loot cavity)
#
# Composition: K 54 (32.5%), M 112 (67.5%), no W. 166 solid cells, one island.
# The shell is the SKIN (thin casing); the meat is the BULK it encloses.

# MIRRORED 2026-08-24 (owner: "it is attacking with its meaty side and hurt
# itself to death"): a creature's drawn facing follows its motion with the +x
# side LEADING, so the old tip-LEFT/mouth-RIGHT authoring led with the MOUTH on
# every ram and the meat paid the bill. Flipped: the armored shell tip is now on
# the RIGHT (+x, leading -- squids jet mantle-first, tentacles trailing) and the
# exposed mouth/meat trails on the LEFT. Directional words in the prose above
# predate the flip; trust the grid.

# HEADERS (2026-09-05) — what this file already was, said out loud, so the
# drafting table can file it. Header lines only: the grid below is untouched.
name Ammonite Kraken
kind kraken

origin 10 4

